; The resident warm test worker — a standalone BYTECODE binary the `fennec dev` supervisor spawns
; once and drives over a Unix socket (see ../test_worker.ml). It links the stable web-test
; FRAMEWORK with -linkall so every framework unit is present for the child's Dynlink to resolve
; against; the app's own libs + the test module are Dynlinked per edit in a fresh fork, never linked
; here. Bytecode only — Dynlink loads .cmo/.cma, and bytecode pays the macOS new-Mach-O dyld/code-sign
; tax just once (at boot), which is the entire point.
;
; The library list is the example web-test framework CLOSURE (computed from `dune describe`): the
; set of project framework libs any fur SSR test transitively needs, MINUS the watched app libs (those
; are the Dynlinked ones). It is mirrored by Test_worker.preloaded so Test_chain can pre-emptively
; decide warm-vs-cold; a test_worker inline test asserts the two stay in sync.
;
; fennec.pulse.live.client is a VIRTUAL library; we pin its .native implementation explicitly so
; -linkall + the fennec umbrella cannot drag the .browser impl in (its top-level Js_of_ocaml code
; aborts a native bytecode process with `caml_pure_js_expr`).
(executable
 (name fennec_test_worker)
 (modes byte)
 (link_flags (-linkall))
 (libraries
  unix
  dynlink
  fennec
  fennec-paw
  fennec-mongo.bson
  fennec-mongo.bson_json
  fennec-mongo.driver
  fennec-mongo.query
  fennec-mongo.minimongo
  fennec-mongo.burrow
  fennec-mongo.backend
  fennec-mongo.dynamic
  fennec-mongo.json
  fennec-mongo.wire
  fennec.accounts
  fennec.accounts.client
  fennec.accounts.features
  fennec.accounts.primitives
  fennec.ddp
  fennec.mail
  fennec.web
  fennec.fur
  fennec.fur.form
  fennec.fur.handler
  fennec.fur.html
  fennec.fur.platform
  fennec.fur.server
  fennec.pulse.live
  fennec.pulse.live.client
  fennec.pulse.live.client.native
  fennec.pulse.method
  fennec.pulse.sift
  fennec.pulse.sift.mongo))
